               </castList>
               The Play of <hi rend="italic">Julius Caesar</hi> is printed conformably to the representation, and<lb/>
               will be to be had [<hi rend="italic">only at the Theatre</hi>] this Evening.<lb/>
               After which will be performed, <hi rend="italic">for the third time</hi>, a New <hi rend="allcaps">Musical Farce</hi> (in two acts) called<lb/>
               <bibl><title ref="namedentities.xml#play_frost_and_thaw">Frost and Thaw.</title></bibl><lb/>
               <hi rend="italic">With new Musick, Scenery, Dresses and Decorations.</hi><lb/>
               <hi rend="italic">The Overture and the whole of the Musick composed by <persName ref="namedentities.xml#th_si_co">Mr. T. <hi rend="allcaps">Cooke</hi></persName>.</hi><lb/>
